From f701f9009ddade049cc4fd66a55be6bc52552eac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: molintc <marek.olczak@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:15:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add direct XPU coverage for FBGEMM lookup operators

Exercise dense lookup forward and split rowwise Adagrad forward plus in-place update through torch.ops without constructing or modifying the FBGEMM TBE frontend. Keep this patch test-only so the installed fbgemm-gpu-cpu runtime remains pristine.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../test/tbe/training/xpu_lookup_ops_test.py  | 221 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 221 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 fbgemm_gpu/test/tbe/training/xpu_lookup_ops_test.py

diff --git a/fbgemm_gpu/test/tbe/training/xpu_lookup_ops_test.py b/fbgemm_gpu/test/tbe/training/xpu_lookup_ops_test.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c60c537
--- /dev/null
+++ b/fbgemm_gpu/test/tbe/training/xpu_lookup_ops_test.py
@@ -0,0 +1,221 @@
